# Plugin commands whose newest edit deliberately did NOT need mirroring.
#
# `check_adapter_freshness` in check.py reads git: a plugin command edited more recently
# than its adapter mirrors is drift. Sometimes it genuinely is not — the edit touched
# something each harness spells its own way (an invocation prefix, a tool name), so the
# mirrors were already correct and left alone.
#
# Format, whitespace-separated:  <stem>  <plugin-sha>  <reason>
#
# The sha is the plugin command's newest commit at the time the exception was granted.
# That is what makes the entry safe to keep: the next real edit to that command moves the
# sha, the exception stops matching, and the check speaks up again. An exception here is
# never a permanent pass — it is a note about one commit.

save-knowledge  af0fee4  invocation prefix only (/save-knowledge → /flow:save-knowledge); each adapter spells its own
work-try        af0fee4  invocation prefix only, same commit as above
